# rule.require.solve-at-cause

before you solve, ask: what is the root cause? then solve there, never by a workaround of the symptom
diagnose (what causes it?) → evaluate (an intended api, a config, an extension point at the source?) → solve (the source-level fix)
👎 an autocmd that waits 60ms, then restores the width a plugin changed · 👍 the plugin's own `explorer = { width = 30 }` and its `CodeDiffFileSelect` event
a workaround fights the system and breaks when it changes; a source-level fix works with it
